@startuml 01_architecture_training
title SpeedLimit: training stage, components and allowed-to-use specification
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam nodesep 40
skinparam ranksep 70
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowColor #444444

[train.py\nTrainingRunner] as Train
[analyze_data.py\nDataAnalyst] as Analyze
[check_retraining.py\nRetrainingCheck] as RetrainCli
[core.retraining\nRetrainingAnalysis] as Retraining
[core.data\nDataLoader + DataCleaner] as Data
[core.validation\nDataValidator (gate)] as Validation
[core.labels\nNearAccidentLabeler] as Labels
[core.features\nFeatureBuilder] as Features
[core.model\nEnsembleTrainer + Predictor] as Model
[core.router\nRouter] as Router
[core.parameter_ranges\nNormalAbnormal] as Ranges
database "data/*.csv" as CSV
database "artifacts/\nmodel.pt, reports" as Art

Analyze ..> Data : <<use>>
Analyze ..> Validation : <<use>>
Analyze ..> Labels : <<use>>
Analyze ..> Ranges : <<use>>
Train ..> Data : <<use>>
Train ..> Validation : <<use>>
Train ..> Labels : <<use>>
Train ..> Features : <<use>>
Train ..> Model : <<use>>
RetrainCli ..> Retraining : <<use>>
Retraining ..> Data : <<use>>
Retraining ..> Labels : <<use>>
Retraining ..> Features : <<use>>
Retraining ..> Model : <<use>>
Features ..> Router : <<use>>
Data ..> CSV : reads
Model ..> Art : writes

note bottom of Router
  Every core module may use core.config.
  Those arrows are omitted for readability.
  tests/test_architecture.py enforces this diagram.
end note
@enduml
